comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-04T11:46:01.044Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete live all-status corpus returned 2873 of 2873 records with zero omissions. Exact GH-1391 and issue URL were absent. Full relevant terminal predecessor metadata and comments were inspected. Request-specific search and open/in-progress inventories were refreshed. This distinct reported boundary is retained under the existing lineage and remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-08T04:24:15.408Z","harness:codex","{\"created_at\": \"now\", \"text\": \"Implementation decision: preserve the source-tracker safety contract instead of admitting none-mode in a live source checkout. Snapshot mode now carries an independent Git object store with exact HEAD/tag identity plus existing nested installation paths, no origin remote, source-local configuration, hooks or shared objects. Original source files and uncommitted package files still copy through the existing containment rules. Real fixture acceptance runs the same package test directly and via CLI-linked snapshot: two dependency versions, a release tag and nested disposable pm init all pass. Forcing schema mode redirects the nested fixture and fails as an intentional negative control. A Git-identity test fails before / passes after; a linked worktree and conflicting ambient GIT_DIR are also covered. The implementation documents excluded working-tree data, historical Git-object visibility and remaining absolute-path/submodule/dependency-write limits. No unsafe source bypass or new command flag is introduced.\"}"
  "2026-10-08T04:48:09.203Z","harness:codex","Manual packed SDK acceptance passes under Node 22.18.0, 24.12.0, 26.9.0 and Bun 1.4.2. Each run initializes an external disposable project via PmClient, adds and runs a tag-aware self-isolating gate through runTest in snapshot mode, verifies nested fixture settings and unchanged source tracker settings, refuses live-source none mode, and certifies the complete SDK corpus. Published 2026.10.8 independently passes npm/Bun 11-step installed journeys and npx/bunx CLI plus stdio/HTTP MCP discovery; those publication receipts do not certify this branch as published."
  "2026-10-08T05:31:54.764Z","harness:codex","Pre-close evidence: all selected PM-linked commands passed. Full source coverage passed 788 files and 9910 tests, exact statements 67214/67214, branches 51435/51435, functions 13854/13854, lines 64042/64042. Two Windows-only cases are delegated to the required Windows gate. Documentation, TypeScript and tracked secret gates passed. Hosted review and final aggregate static validation remain delivery checks; no publication of this branch is claimed."
  "2026-10-08T05:59:25.852Z","harness:codex","Final delivery verification: packed npm/npx/bunx smoke passed with nine packages; all selected linked commands passed. Full source coverage reports 9910 passing tests and exact 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. The static aggregate stopped on metadata and prose-edge gaps; after CLI repairs its tracker-context, graph-composition, record-integrity and mutation components pass, with 329 killed mutants and seven reviewed equivalents. Required hosted aggregate validation and review remain pending; this branch is not published."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-08T04:51:13.863Z","harness:codex","Snapshot acceptance decision: preserve the original tag-aware gate in an independent Git clone rather than permit unprotected live-source execution with PM_PATH unset. Fresh config, empty template, no shared objects, removed origin and contained file aliases preserve the source boundary. Dependencies retain original nested lookup identities. Snapshot Git history is intentionally not redacted; source-local settings, absolute paths and submodule configuration are documented limits."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-08T04:51:16.231Z","harness:codex",A faithful package gate needs independent Git identity as well as files and dependencies. Explicitly removing PM_PATH fixes nested init targeting only when the disposable temporary ancestry itself has no initialized tracker.
